\textbf{Inclusion criteria:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Studies addressing sustainability in software development or software-intensive organizations.
    \item Studies providing empirical evidence on sustainability implementation practices, organizational arrangements, or factors affecting implementation.
    \item Studies addressing environmental or other sustainability dimensions with a clear connection to software engineering.
    \item Studies using empirical methods, such as surveys, interviews, case studies, experiments, mixed methods, or repository and artifact analyses.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Exclusion criteria:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Conceptual, theoretical, or vision papers without empirical evidence.
    \item Proposed frameworks or methods without empirical evaluation.
    \item Studies focusing only on software maintainability, longevity, or quality without an explicit sustainability perspective.
    \item Studies discussing sustainability at a general organizational level without a clear connection to software development or software-intensive organizations.
    \item Duplicate records.
\end{itemize}
